    "stac_version": "1.1.0",
    "description": "Deschampsia antarctica plants were collected in Robert Island, Antarctica, and\nfrozen in liquid nitrogen. Polar lipids and the composition of fatty acids in\nphospholipids and galactolipids were analysed in leaves and roots. Compared to\nother Gramineae, no unusual contents in polar lipids and in the degree of no\nsaturation of fatty acids in most lipid fractions were found. The highest\nunsaturation ratio (unsaturated/saturated fatty acids) of 3.3 was found in the\nphosphatidylinositol fraction. Although summer environmental temperatures in\nRobert Island are usually around 0 degrees, leaves often reach higher\ntemperatures, which are near their photosynthetic optimum.",
